1
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:03,420
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:32,010
[birds chirping]

3
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,840
[door opens]

4
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,510
-[Yuru gasps]
-[HANA] Come on in.

5
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:40,140
[Left and Right exclaim]

6
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,890
I wondered
what those stone castles

7
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:44,940
would look like from the inside.

8
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:47,400
Electricity and water
are already set up.

9
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:50,190
Somebody's gonna come by
to turn on the gas later.

10
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:51,320
[doorknob rattles]

11
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:54,240
[HANA] Dera, you can use
that Western-style room.

12
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,870
Yuru, you'll want
the tatami room, right?

13
00:01:56,910 --> 00:02:00,500
Tatami? [gasps, exclaims]

14
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:01,960
This stuff's real!

15
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,920
Back in the village,
tatami are only used by Asa.

16
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,580
Or for very special events!

17
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:08,380
They usually use
goza mats, right?

18
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:11,470
Ah! [chuckles] They must have
a million layers,

19
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:13,380
with how thick each one feels!

20
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:15,380
We're living a life
of luxury here!

21
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,890
Are you sure I'm allowed
to sleep in this room?

22
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:19,470
-[footsteps]
-Hm?

23
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:22,730
[smacking]

24
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:24,850
[Yuru screams]

25
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,060
[HANA] Oh, that's my bad!
Let me introduce you.

26
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:30,110
This is Kotetsu and Jiro!

27
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,610
-[chuckles]
-[YURU] Mm?

28
00:02:31,650 --> 00:02:32,860
Excuse the intrusion.

29
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:34,820
[Yuru gasps]

30
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:38,320
Our gratitude for letting
our master into your home!

31
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:40,490
And we're the daemons
contracted to him.

32
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:42,910
My name is Right. [chuckles]

33
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,500
And mine is Left.

34
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:46,160
Good health to you both.

35
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:48,630
-[KOTETSU] My man.
-[Jiro exclaims]

36
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:50,630
[DERA] Are those Hana's daemons?

37
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:52,970
Nice to finally meet you.

38
00:02:53,010 --> 00:02:56,430
What? Those two are daemons?
That cat and dog?

39
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:59,220
[Yuru screams, grunts]

40
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,640
[RIGHT] They're not
your average cat and dog.

41
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,890
Now show some respect

42
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:05,100
and give 'em a proper greeting,
young one.

43
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,810
You put 'em together,
they're called Zenko-Koro.

44
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:12,110
-[Yuru whimpers]
-[HANA] Say hi!

45
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:13,190
Apologies.

46
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:15,700
[YURU] Hello.

47
00:03:16,950 --> 00:03:18,120
[YURU] Danno?

48
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,530
I feel like we should use
my family name,

49
00:03:20,570 --> 00:03:23,160
since somebody
let his identity slip.

50
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:25,160
Yeah, sorry. Good call.

51
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,500
[HANA] If anyone asks,
this is also your name.

52
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,790
Wait, you both have
family names?

53
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,380
Do you come from royalty?

54
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:33,670
Have I been disrespectful
to you, too?

55
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:36,380
Relax, kid. Everyone down here
has a last name.

56
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,890
Don't be fooled.
She owns a mountain!

57
00:03:38,930 --> 00:03:40,010
She's a lord?

58
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:42,390
It's just something that got
passed down from my family!

59
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:45,770
There's no one maintaining it,
so it's an overgrown mess.

60
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:47,900
But I can't exactly
sell it, either.

61
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:49,940
[YURU] So, may I go
hunting there?

62
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,230
[Hana sighs] Don't say that
like it's normal.

63
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:54,400
[DERA] Down here, you need
to have a license to hunt.

64
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,740
-[YURU] Why?
-[DERA] Hey, you just do.

65
00:03:56,780 --> 00:03:57,990
You'll need a separate one

66
00:03:58,030 --> 00:04:00,660
if you wanna drive
those metal horses, too.

67
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,990
[YURU] This world
has so many rules.

68
00:04:03,490 --> 00:04:05,500
♪

69
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,010
[ASA] Hmm.

70
00:04:29,230 --> 00:04:30,270
[Asa grunts]

71
00:04:33,650 --> 00:04:36,690
[Asa groans]
Still struggling to tune it.

72
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:37,820
-[GONZO] Hm.
-[Asa gasps]

73
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,860
[GONZO] Look at you,
hard at work!

74
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:41,280
[ASA] Master, you're back!

75
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,530
Yup!

76
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:46,700
[ASA] My apologies.

77
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:48,540
I brought harm
to your land again.

78
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,460
My accuracy still needs
improvement.

79
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,420
Oh, it's just a yard.

80
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:54,380
It's not as if
you killed anyone.

81
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:56,460
Keep trying,
and you'll get there.

82
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,210
Now, Jin, clean that up for us.

83
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,800
Yes, sir.

84
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,220
Ai, my dear?

85
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,770
[Ai growls]

86
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,270
Is there a reason
you came to visit?

87
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:16,730
Hm. Got a "get better" gift
for Gabby! [chuckles]

88
00:05:16,770 --> 00:05:17,900
What?

89
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,490
You don't need to waste
your time worrying 'bout me.

90
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:22,490
How are you feeling, sweetie?

91
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,910
[GABBY] Not half bad.
Thanks for askin'.

92
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:27,620
And how are you holding up,
Gabriel?

93
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,580
[Gabriel grunts]

94
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,830
Hm. Yes. Of course, of course!

95
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:33,290
Hey, Gabby, you want
a little snack?

96
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:34,380
[GABBY] Apple me!

97
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:37,920
Oh, but I don't have a knife
to cut it the way you like.

98
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,170
Makoto.

99
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,470
[Makoto grunts]

100
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:44,090
For you.

101
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:45,640
Thanks to both of you.

102
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,760
How nice of you,

103
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:49,470
cutting up that apple with
a knife of dubious origin.

104
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,270
You really expect me
to eat that?

105
00:05:51,730 --> 00:05:52,890
[JIN] It's all right.

106
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:55,230
It hasn't stabbed anyone.
Probably.

107
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:57,360
[GABBY] I am so reassured.

108
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:05,280
Now, Gabby, please focus
on rest and recovery.

109
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,740
[GABBY] 'Kay.

110
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,240
And as for you, Asa,

111
00:06:08,290 --> 00:06:10,000
-I want you to stay with her.
-[ASA] Huh?

112
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,450
With you and your brother
both off the mountain,

113
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:15,500
it's safe to say word is gonna
start getting around fast.

114
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:18,000
That means people
will soon be after you.

115
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:20,800
Even just looking
within the Kagemori clan,

116
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:23,220
there are some
targeting you, I fear.

117
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:25,970
But as long as you're here,
I can keep you safe.

118
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,930
I've instructed Jin
to continue searching for Yuru.

119
00:06:28,970 --> 00:06:30,010
Understood?

120
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,020
Yes, sir.

121
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,850
One small problem.

122
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:36,020
I don't even know what this
big brother looks like.

123
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:40,110
Ah... we should have snapped
a pic while we were there!

124
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:41,780
[scribbling]

125
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:43,820
-Here!
-[JIN] Seems biased.

126
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,030
-[Gabby yells]
-[JIN] Abstract.

127
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,280
Whoa, Flawless?

128
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:48,490
[clears throat]

129
00:06:48,570 --> 00:06:50,830
I'll begin the search
by looking into Tadera.

130
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:52,540
Don't disappoint!

131
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,500
[footsteps]

132
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,290
[ASA] Before you go...

133
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,380
Is something wrong?

134
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:03,010
My brother's daemons
have keen noses.

135
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:04,550
-[JIN] Hm.
-They could identify me

136
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:06,260
from the smell of my blood.

137
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:08,760
[Jin gasps softly]

138
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,470
[JIN] Incredible.

139
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:16,310
[DERA] Oh, yeah!

140
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:18,400
I'm a new man!

141
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,360
Hold up. Where'd your beard go?

142
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,990
They saw my face,
so I had to shave it.

143
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:27,360
Every little bit,
to throw 'em off the scent!

144
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:30,240
You lost your only similarity
to Jason Statham.

145
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,910
You're dead to me now.

146
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:33,540
We just tied the knot,

147
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:36,080
and my wife's
already lost interest.

148
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:42,670
Do you know where our pride
and joy ran off to?

149
00:07:42,710 --> 00:07:44,340
[HANA] If you're talking
about Yuru,

150
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,590
he said he was going for a walk
to get the lay of the land.

151
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,380
Think he'll be okay?

152
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:50,260
[HANA] He's got
Left and Right with him.

153
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:51,890
I'm sure he'll be fine.

154
00:07:52,850 --> 00:07:55,430
[DERA] Hana,
where's my billhook?

155
00:07:55,470 --> 00:07:57,560
[HANA] Don't ask me.
I didn't touch it.

156
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:00,020
[DERA] I'm sure
I left it by the door.

157
00:08:00,690 --> 00:08:02,020
Ah, crap.

158
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,610
Wonder how far he went.

159
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,110
-[Hana grunts]
-If the cops find him,

160
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:09,280
he's in violation

161
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:11,660
of the Firearms
and Swords Control Act.

162
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,990
[HANA] I told him
to stay out of trouble!

163
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:16,040
I hate kids!

164
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:21,830
The world below sure is big.

165
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:24,710
The stars reach
all the way to the ground.

166
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:26,800
It's massive.

167
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:29,090
[RIGHT] Does the vastness
concern you?

168
00:08:29,130 --> 00:08:30,970
Is it you fear
it will be impossible

169
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:33,680
to find a singular person
in this world?

170
00:08:34,350 --> 00:08:36,640
I have no doubt
that your paths shall meet.

171
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,640
She's seeking you out as well.

172
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:39,940
[laughs]

173
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:42,230
How quaint!
Power of sibling love!

174
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:43,560
♪

175
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,070
Can't you sense daemons?

176
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:50,280
Like how you did before
with Oshirasama.

177
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:52,410
Was that just by smell?

178
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:53,950
Aye.

179
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:56,410
[YURU] And you said
this Asa's blood

180
00:08:56,450 --> 00:08:57,660
smelled like mine?

181
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:58,830
Aye.

182
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:03,080
[YURU] Dera said the Kagemoris
have many daemon wielders.

183
00:09:03,130 --> 00:09:04,630
Not just the runt.

184
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:07,460
So that's what
we're looking for.

185
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:10,760
A place with daemons
that smells of my blood, yeah?

186
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,350
That's enough to begin.

187
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,470
Let's go!

188
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:16,720
♪

189
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:23,310
[Right laughs]

190
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:26,400
[RIGHT] We'll up the sensitivity
a notch!

191
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,780
♪

192
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:34,070
[Yuru screams]

193
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:36,410
[Yuru screams, laughs]

194
00:09:42,710 --> 00:09:44,420
[Yuru shouts indistinctly]

195
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,640
[Yuru vomits, coughs]

196
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:01,600
[Yuru whimpers]

197
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:04,690
Blood like yours and daemons.

198
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:06,150
I believe we have unearthed

199
00:10:06,190 --> 00:10:07,440
-a perfect match.
-[Yuru groans]

200
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:09,940
There's daemons here?
You're sure?

201
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:12,110
Have we permission
to cut them down

202
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:14,200
should they dare
to show themselves?

203
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:16,490
Shouldn't we at least
try to speak with them first,

204
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:18,450
in case they're friendly
like Oshirasama?

205
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,040
You'd be wise
not to measure daemons

206
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,290
by the same standards as humans.

207
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:25,620
We're too varied
to relate to one another.

208
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:28,130
Some have no means
to process reason.

209
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:29,670
Interesting.

210
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,670
So I should think of them
like bears, or wild boar.

211
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,010
[RIGHT] Simpleton.

212
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:36,300
Huh? [sniffs]

213
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:37,550
[YURU] Hm?

214
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:41,560
♪

215
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,320
[JIN] You found it?

216
00:10:57,370 --> 00:10:58,740
Ah, I see.

217
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:00,120
Then I'm sure Mr. Tadera

218
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,370
must have already
cleared out the space.

219
00:11:02,410 --> 00:11:03,410
Yep.

220
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:06,420
I want to be the first to know
if you hear anything.

221
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:09,880
Ah, the smell of Asa
is only matched

222
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:12,590
by the smell of those
daemons of theirs.

223
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:15,590
Though, we must be sure
to stay on our guard.

224
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:17,010
If we've noticed them,

225
00:11:17,050 --> 00:11:19,850
no doubt they've caught
wind of us, too.

226
00:11:19,890 --> 00:11:21,680
-[RIGHT] See anything?
-[YURU] No, nothing.

227
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:25,350
Those guys in black are humans,
right?

228
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:26,940
[RIGHT] Seem to be.

229
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:30,020
-[Right sniffs]
-[LEFT] Hm?

230
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:31,440
♪

231
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:38,030
[Yuru gasps]

232
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,410
[Yuru grunts]

233
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,080
Asa!

234
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,160
Wait, Yuru!

235
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:47,670
The blood's scent is aged!
She's not...

236
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,390
According to my sources,

237
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,680
your daemons have
a strong sense of smell.

238
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:09,650
Furthermore, since you reacted
so strongly to this Asa...

239
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:13,150
it seems I've caught
her brother.

240
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:17,240
How do you do, kid?
The name's Jin Kagemori.

241
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:21,370
These here are my daemons,
the Scavenger.

242
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:25,160
It's a pleasure to make
your acquaintance, Yuru.

243
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,540
[Yuru grunts softly]

244
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,540
[HANA] Shit. Shit, shit, shit!

245
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:35,550
We gotta find out
where Yuru is ASAP.

246
00:12:35,590 --> 00:12:37,130
[DERA] I'd say so.

247
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:39,170
He still doesn't know
the ways of our world,

248
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,970
so he might wind up
hurting someone.

249
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,220
-[Hana grunts]
-[Dera gasps]

250
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:43,800
[HANA] That's just one problem.

251
00:12:43,850 --> 00:12:46,430
But what are we gonna do
if he's the one who gets hurt?

252
00:12:47,430 --> 00:12:49,980
Wait, what happened
to Miss Hates-Children?

253
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:51,400
Seems like you're
awfully worried

254
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,560
about how our boy's doing!

255
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:53,650
[HANA] What?

256
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,820
Are you willfully ignorant,
or dumb?

257
00:12:55,860 --> 00:12:57,150
-[DERA] Huh?
-[HANA] Last I checked,

258
00:12:57,190 --> 00:12:59,110
the kid isn't
a registered citizen yet.

259
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:01,200
Yeah, obviously.

260
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:04,200
His hometown
is a bit behind the times.

261
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,450
Hold on.

262
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:07,370
Doesn't that mean...

263
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:10,790
[BOTH] He's got
no health insurance.

264
00:13:10,830 --> 00:13:13,500
So we're on the hook
for any medical bills!

265
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:14,790
-Shit, shit, shit...
-Jiro.

266
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,090
[Jiro barks]

267
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,590
This thing ought
to smell like Yuru.

268
00:13:18,630 --> 00:13:20,920
-Let's track him down!
-[Jiro sniffs]

269
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:23,010
[Jiro grunts]

270
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,430
We're counting on you!

271
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,470
[Jiro barking]

272
00:13:29,180 --> 00:13:31,730
[Jiro howls]

273
00:13:32,310 --> 00:13:34,230
[HANA] Kotetsu, your turn.

274
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:35,400
[Kotetsu grunts]

275
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:40,400
Well, would you look at that.

276
00:13:40,450 --> 00:13:42,360
Your daemons can use
modern tech?

277
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:44,620
[HANA] They adapted
to living around here.

278
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:46,580
They've been in my family
for generations,

279
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:48,120
so it was bound to happen.

280
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:51,370
So then? Where did our
good boy run off to?

281
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:52,460
Huh?

282
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:53,630
How the hell did he get

283
00:13:53,670 --> 00:13:55,170
all the way to Tokyo
in one night?

284
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,880
Damn, kid. Wasting no time.

285
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:00,210
[HANA] Left and Right
must've taken him.

286
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:01,840
[DERA] Is he lost?

287
00:14:02,130 --> 00:14:06,300
No. Maybe he had a good reason
to go there.

288
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:08,390
♪

289
00:14:09,770 --> 00:14:12,640
[JIN] You may think we're crazy
for chasing you twins,

290
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:15,730
but the Higashi Village elders
are just as bad.

291
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:18,150
That said, they're recovering
from our attack,

292
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:21,030
and you're freshly on the run,
so things are peaceful.

293
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,900
Surely they wouldn't stage
a counterattack already.

294
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,910
But I'm sure they know
we're thinking that

295
00:14:26,950 --> 00:14:29,080
and expect us
to let down our guard.

296
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,450
I couldn't rule it out.

297
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:33,750
So I laid this trap
for one of them to fall into.

298
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:36,290
The fact we got you was lucky.

299
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,710
Thanks for that,
Mr. Big Brother.

300
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:40,800
[Yuru grunts]

301
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:46,050
[YURU] Too tough.

302
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:48,680
Hey, daemons,
you're hiding, right?

303
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,890
Come on out.

304
00:14:53,390 --> 00:14:54,730
Thoughts, Left?

305
00:14:54,770 --> 00:14:57,730
I don't detect the scent of iron
wafting off them.

306
00:14:57,770 --> 00:15:00,480
It would appear this lot
is unarmed, at least.

307
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,860
Though I do still sense
their daemons.

308
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,280
The fish and four more.

309
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,870
The other pairs
must belong to them.

310
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:10,280
They're hiding until
we make the first move,

311
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:11,790
waiting to see what we do.

312
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,370
[both grunt softly]

313
00:15:14,750 --> 00:15:17,790
[Right grunts]

314
00:15:21,250 --> 00:15:22,630
[RIGHT] Oh, well.

315
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:25,760
Whatever happens happens.

316
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,050
[HARUO] There, look!

317
00:15:27,090 --> 00:15:29,050
Stay right where you are!

318
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:32,100
We will kill your master
if you do not comply!

319
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:35,310
We're happy to give him back,
as long as you guys... [gasps]

320
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:38,730
Hey, stop!

321
00:15:38,770 --> 00:15:42,190
Hey! Are you listening to me?
Don't you dare come any closer!

322
00:15:42,230 --> 00:15:44,610
I'm telling you
your master is our hostage!

323
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:46,950
And which one should be
our hostage?

324
00:15:46,990 --> 00:15:48,110
The sullen one.

325
00:15:48,150 --> 00:15:50,120
Seems he's in charge.

326
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:52,790
[HARUO] Come on, guys!
I said stop!

327
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:57,210
My apologies, you two.
I lost my head back there.

328
00:15:57,250 --> 00:15:59,920
[RIGHT] Eh, can't blame you
for that one.

329
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,880
Just be sure to stay put.

330
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,710
Mm? Why should I?

331
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:05,630
This fish thing looks powerful.

332
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:07,800
As long as it's busy
being your jail cell,

333
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,050
it can't fight us.

334
00:16:09,090 --> 00:16:12,390
Oh. I can accept that.
Works for me.

335
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:13,640
What did they say?

336
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:15,770
Why are the daemons
giving orders to their master?

337
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:17,600
You guys are
supposed to prioritize

338
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,940
rescuing your master
over everything else!

339
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:22,150
[YURU] Nah,
I'm pretty hands-off.

340
00:16:22,610 --> 00:16:25,940
[laughs] You've got your way,
we've got ours!

341
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:29,610
Remember, our opponents
have no weapons.

342
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:31,120
We should take it easy on them.

343
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,280
I ought to be the one
telling you that.

344
00:16:33,330 --> 00:16:34,410
But sure.

345
00:16:34,450 --> 00:16:36,160
Give us a hand.

346
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:39,580
[Yuru gasps]

347
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:41,630
[YURU] Careful of those weapons.

348
00:16:47,470 --> 00:16:48,760
[Jin grunts softly]

349
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,470
[RIGHT] Huh?

350
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,720
You bid us be careful of what?

351
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:55,680
We're sculpted of stone,
far tougher than that.

352
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:58,350
[chuckles awkwardly]
Yeah, of course.

353
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,360
How annoying.

354
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,070
What do you suppose these are?

355
00:17:07,110 --> 00:17:09,240
They remind me of matchlocks.

356
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,530
♪

357
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:12,910
[Haruo grunts]

358
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,660
[grunts] Keep tryin'.
It ain't workin'.

359
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:19,830
[Makoto grunts]

360
00:17:20,910 --> 00:17:21,960
[Right grunts]

361
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:24,210
[LEFT] Was that a lantern?

362
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:40,430
Actually,
they're quite well-armed.

363
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:42,190
Don't gotta hold back.

364
00:17:42,230 --> 00:17:43,440
Agreed.

365
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,480
Aw, crap. Out of the way, Akio!
I got you!

366
00:17:50,610 --> 00:17:52,150
You all right?

367
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:58,120
[Right grunting]

368
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,790
[Right grunts]

369
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,670
[Right grunting]
What's going on?

370
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:11,380
Come on, Left, help me!

371
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,800
[LEFT] Apologies, Right. Busy.

372
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,310
I can't move.

373
00:18:19,060 --> 00:18:20,270
'Tis heavy.

374
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:22,020
'Tis so very heavy.

375
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:27,190
Truly? [screams]

376
00:18:27,230 --> 00:18:28,650
Please save me, Left!

377
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:31,030
[LEFT] I cannot. Save yourself.

378
00:18:34,910 --> 00:18:36,370
♪

379
00:18:37,370 --> 00:18:38,700
[Yuru grunts softly]

380
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:41,870
[Yuru grunts]

381
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:44,870
[YURU] That's it.

382
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,380
Yuru, stay clear!

383
00:19:00,510 --> 00:19:01,890
[Ai screams]

384
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:03,810
Less tough than the other teeth.

385
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,650
[Yuru grunts]

386
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:08,480
Right!

387
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:11,440
When you leave the latrine, you?

388
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,610
[Right grunts]

389
00:19:12,990 --> 00:19:15,950
[RIGHT] Kill the lights!

390
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:29,000
-[BUNBUN] Haruo, where are you?
-Over here.

391
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:31,710
I sense the boy's daemons moving
further away from us

392
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:33,010
with each passing second.

393
00:19:33,050 --> 00:19:34,380
[HARUO] They got away?

394
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:38,180
[JIN] No. Akio's daemons
are lying in wait.

395
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:40,510
If you think
you're getting away that easy,

396
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:41,760
you're dead wrong.

397
00:19:41,810 --> 00:19:43,310
You should see him.

398
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,310
He's got the mind
of a die-hard hunter!

399
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:47,310
[Jin grunts softly]

400
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:50,020
-[whooshes]
-[Jin grunts]

401
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,570
[grunts] Makoto, light!

402
00:19:55,230 --> 00:19:56,440
♪

403
00:20:05,290 --> 00:20:06,750
[Jin breathes uneasily]

404
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:12,090
-Oy! Did it work out?
-[Haruo gasps] Hey!

405
00:20:12,130 --> 00:20:13,460
What's your deal?

406
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:16,670
Daemons shouldn't abandon
their master! You ran!

407
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,050
[RIGHT] Bah...

408
00:20:18,090 --> 00:20:19,840
I don't know what you guys do,

409
00:20:19,890 --> 00:20:22,510
but this is what we've found
works for us.

410
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:25,430
We may do as we please
as long as the job gets done.

411
00:20:25,470 --> 00:20:28,600
Huh? Doesn't it make sense
to run away from a trap

412
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,640
when you can?

413
00:20:29,690 --> 00:20:31,190
Better than all dying.

414
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,400
Uh, suppose you have a point.

415
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:35,940
Your surprise makes me think
you've forgotten.

416
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:38,650
But of the twins,
our Yuru commands the night.

417
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:41,530
[LEFT] The darkness
is his hunting ground.

418
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:43,700
He can manage fine without us.

419
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:44,910
[Haruo gasps]

420
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:47,370
I totally love how much faith
you have in him.

421
00:20:47,410 --> 00:20:49,040
That rocks.

422
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:51,790
Had Yuru failed to secure
his prey, though,

423
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:53,750
we would have swept in
to assist him.

424
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:56,130
Even in the murk,
we can track your scent.

425
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:57,630
Only natural.

426
00:20:57,710 --> 00:21:00,180
You grew up in
a mountain village, after all.

427
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:01,380
In a battle of senses,

428
00:21:01,430 --> 00:21:04,140
you have an undeniable advantage
over us.

429
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,890
You said you're a Kagemori.

430
00:21:06,430 --> 00:21:09,560
Is your clan responsible
for the attack on Higashi?

431
00:21:14,860 --> 00:21:16,690
[JIN] I alone am responsible.

432
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:19,440
-[both gasp]
-No, don't!

433
00:21:20,950 --> 00:21:22,240
♪

434
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:25,490
[breathing shakily]

435
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:34,960
[Yuru sighs]

436
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:39,300
[YURU] You've got one of those
smoke signal things, right?

437
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,380
[JIN] Hm?

438
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:43,640
The device that lets you talk
to people far away.

439
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,850
I saw you were using it earlier.

440
00:21:45,890 --> 00:21:47,850
Oh, you mean my smartphone.

441
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,930
You're gonna tell Asa
to come here.

442
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:53,980
I just want to talk, that's all.

443
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

444
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:30,120
Gabby! Gabby! Gabby!
Gabby! Gabby! Gabby!

445
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:32,700
Jin is bringing
my brother here.

446
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:35,830
Our parents boarded
the plane to Okinawa,

447
00:23:35,870 --> 00:23:36,830
but didn't land.

448
00:23:36,870 --> 00:23:38,000
They're gone.
